WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.560
- I wanna bring this
up, because a while ago

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.240
you gave a commencement speech at Harvard

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.130
which is incredibly cool,
and you said something

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.072
that was really cool.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.920
- Yeah, many ago.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.450
- So you said, "As you
navigate through the rest

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.790
of your life, be open to collaborations.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.580
Other people's ideas are
often better than your own.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.220
Find a group of people who
challenge and inspire you,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.250
spend a lot of time with them
and it will change your life."

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.453
I think this is the best advice.

00:00:22.453 --> 00:00:23.340
(audience applauding)

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.630
- Thank you.
- It is.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.340
People always, I don't even
if they look at you go,

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.230
oh my God, your career, you've
done so well, I'm like, yeah,

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.930
a team of people like
there's a whole group of us

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.280
that have made all of this happen.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.280
Like it's so smart to tell people to do.

00:00:35.117 --> 00:00:37.170
- I think you can do
anything with a good team,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.250
- Yeah.
- You can do anything.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.490
And a good team is a team
that everyone feels like

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.560
they know what they're working for.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.910
And also there's not a lot
of like, that's not my job.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.280
A good team is a team that works together.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.370
I've been really lucky in my
life to be on many of them.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.620
And I feel like because of that

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.180
I've been able to do all
these different things.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.730
If you have a team of people,
and it's could be your family,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.020
your partner, the people you work with

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.150
you have people who know you, support you.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.290
care about you can do anything.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.540
And there's no better feeling than like

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.280
failing and successing like,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.113
success and failure with someone.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.530
It feels so good to win as a team.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.700
- Yeah.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.968
And it's a lot less lonely
when you when you fail

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.600
- When you fail, yeah, and we all do,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.370
that's the thing, I think
that people frown upon it,

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.690
but it's like, well
that's the time I think

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.000
you learn the most, not
when you win, so yeah,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:24.986
I think that's all right.

00:01:24.986 --> 00:01:26.880
- And I think that
working well with others

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.880
is a really valuable skill that
I think is really important.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.810
And I know it's important
with the people I work with.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.190
You like to work with other people.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.350
- That's why your shows, a
lot of that is like your shows

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.880
that I love watching, it's
always like, teams and people

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.230
like working together make
something happen at the end,

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.820
and there's a product and it's fun.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.890
- Yeah, I think that's why
workplace comedies are fun

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.330
is 'cause it's a team of people

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.195
that would never choose to be together.

00:01:47.195 --> 00:01:49.170
(Kelly and Amy laughing)

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.970
And you're like, wow, we
have nothing in common.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:51.803
Let's make this happen.

00:01:51.803 --> 00:01:53.069
- And yet we're succeeding.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:53.902
(Kelly and Amy laughing)

